沙星 demonstrate strong interactions with theophylline and related compounds. Evidence shows that 丙氟哌酸, when co-administered with theophylline, leads to significantly elevated theophylline blood concentrations, especially in elderly patients or those with liver impairment [Data: Relationships (27156)]. Furthermore, older fluoroquinolones like 氟啶酸 (not explicitly listed but referenced contextually) can double theophylline plasma concentrations, necessitating dose reduction and therapeutic drug monitoring [Data: Relationships (4215)]. In contrast, newer agents like 洛美沙星 appear to have minimal effect on theophylline clearance, indicating class heterogeneity in interaction potential [Data: Relationships (4215)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Theophylline interacts with dietary and pharmacological agents affecting its clearance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Theophylline’s metabolism is sensitive to both dietary and drug-based modulators. Consumption of 含咖啡因的饮料 (caffeinated beverages) can reduce theophylline efficacy, requiring dosage adjustments; conversely, abrupt cessation may precipitate theophylline toxicity due to unanticipated concentration increases [Data: Relationships (32747)]. Additionally, theophylline is a substrate for organic anion transporters (OATs), and co-administration with drugs like erythromycin (a macrolide) competitively inhibits its renal excretion, elevating blood concentrations and increasing toxicity risk [Data: Relationships (4216)]. These findings underscore the importance of comprehensive patient history regarding diet and concomitant medications when managing theophylline therapy.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Serious adverse reactions linked to fluoroquinolone use\",\n            \"explanation\": \"培氟沙星 is associated with severe musculoskeletal adverse effects, specifically 跟腱炎症 (tendonitis) and 跟腱断裂 (tendon rupture), particularly when used concomitantly with corticosteroids [Data: Relationships (10652, 10654)]. Similarly, 洛美沙星 exhibits 光反应毒性 (phototoxicity), which can manifest as severe skin reactions upon UV exposure [Data: Relationships (13704)]. These adverse reactions are well-documented class effects of fluoroquinolones and carry significant clinical implications, often warranting avoidance in high-risk populations such as the elderly or those on systemic steroids.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Toxicity from drug interactions manifests in measurable clinical symptoms\",\n            \"explanation\": \"中毒 (toxicity) resulting from drug–drug interactions presents with specific neurological and systemic symptoms. For instance, poisoning related to 卡马西平 or theophylline can lead to 共济失调 (ataxia), among other signs like dizziness, nystagmus, and seizures [Data: Relationships (17643)]. Elevated theophylline concentrations—whether from inhibited metabolism (e.g., by macrolides or quinolones) or reduced clearance—are directly linked to life-threatening toxicities including arrhythmias, seizures, and metabolic disturbances like hypokalemia [Data: Relationships (4215, 32747)]. These manifestations necessitate vigilant therapeutic drug monitoring in at-risk patients.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Pharmacokinetic indicators serve as critical markers for interaction severity\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Key pharmacokinetic indicators such as 茶碱清除率, 血浆清除率, and 血浆茶碱浓度 are repeatedly cited as affected endpoints in drug interaction studies. For example, 奥美拉唑 induces CYP1A2 activity, increasing 茶碱清除率 by 11% and reducing its area under the curve (AUC) by 20%, thereby potentially compromising efficacy [Data: Relationships (1838)]. Conversely, inhibitors of CYP1A2 or OAT-mediated excretion elevate 血浆茶碱浓度, raising toxicity risk [Data: Relationships (4207, 4216)]. Monitoring these indicators allows clinicians to preemptively adjust doses and mitigate adverse outcomes.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"r